  "routes": {
    "about": [
      "Which view governs a client route, and who reaches it. An app owns every route below its surfaces:",
      "/x/<slug>/<anything> is the work view's and /x/<slug>/manage/<anything> the manage view's, so a",
      "work-only member reaches /x/crm/a/b and never /x/crm/manage/a, and a manage-only member the reverse.",
      "Paths compare ASCII-case-insensitively, as the client router matches a static segment: it mounts the",
      "manage surface at /x/crm/MANAGE. TS asserts appViewFor and isViewDenied (the route gate and the nav),",
      "and runs the client router's own matcher over its route table for every path (route-table.test.ts);",
      "Rust asserts app_view_for and ViewGrants::denies. Each viewer below is a member holding those app",
      "views, with /teams denied; `open` names the viewers the path is open to. `reservedSlugs` are the",
      "client router's config keys, which install refuses as app slugs (Rust RESERVED_APP_SLUGS, the CLI's",
      "`talaria app new`); an app that already has one still routes, which the hooks and layout paths pin."
    ],
    "viewers": {
      "work": {
        "denied": [
          "/teams"
        ],
        "appGrants": [
          "/x/crm",
          "/x/hooks"
        ]
      },
      "manage": {
        "denied": [
          "/teams"
        ],
        "appGrants": [
          "/x/crm/manage",
          "/x/hooks/manage"
        ]
      },
      "none": {
        "denied": [
          "/teams"
        ],
        "appGrants": []
      }
    },
    "reservedSlugs": [
      "layout",
      "hooks",
      "meta"
    ],
